Your system Python 3.13 had a broken pip install: the package files were missing but `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` remained in `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages`. Because of that `ensurepip` thought pip was already satisfied and never re-installed the code, so `import pip` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`.

I removed the stale metadata and forced a reinstall:

```bash
rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info
python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip
```

Check:

```
$ python3 -c "import pip; print(pip.__file__)"
